# Actor Home and Production Center

Read `docs/ACTOR_HOME_PRODUCTION_UNDERGROUND_CENTER.md` before planning or editing Actor, Production, application, social, discovery, memory, onboarding, or shell behavior.

## Architectural center

```text
Human authority
→ personal Actor / Living Self Page
→ Productions and discovery
→ participating Actors and Actor App Surfaces
→ bounded Agents and adapters
→ Gummies, Returns, Receipts, and approved Actor updates
```

The Human-owned personal Actor is the experiential center. Production is the durable undertaking. Applications extend Actors. Agents perform bounded work. Master Control governs authority and data flow.

Do not make the app launcher, chat transcript, Agent graph, file browser, storage provider, or Production dashboard the sole conceptual center of Gummy OS.

## Locked distinctions

- Human and Actor do not collapse.
- Actor and Agent do not collapse.
- Living Self Page is a surface, not authority.
- Personal, service, Production, organization, and collective Actors may use one protocol without pretending every Actor is a person.
- Production-specific state does not silently become Actor memory.
- Actor learning requires evidence and an ActorUpdateProposal.
- AI-assisted output is not independent Human mastery.
- Actor branches inherit only explicitly selected knowledge references, never ambient authority or private memory.
- Underground is an experience/discovery/spatial layer, not an authority, storage, or protocol substitute.
- Exact cave visuals, wallpapers, crystals, and mandatory 3D navigation are not locked canon without founder approval.

